Settings and navigation fixes from review

- Finance was a dead end with no accounts: the empty state said "create a
  bank account first" while replacing the very tab where accounts are
  created. The create form is now what you land on.
- Company details moved from Profile to Settings. Profile is about the
  user; company data belongs to the organisation.
- Offices can be reactivated. Deleting an office sets isActive=false so
  old references survive, but no form field could set it back — deletion
  was effectively permanent.
- Daily report is a section under System rather than its own tab. Both are
  system settings and both depend on the scheduler.
- Profile and Settings moved into the account menu at the bottom of the
  sidebar, their conventional place. The Settings entry there had been
  disabled with a comment saying its page did not exist yet; it does.

